; WildGrassPalm — 2nd of 3 sand/desert-flavor Wild grass variants (content-variety pass
; Task 9, 2026-08-26). See wild_grass.tres's own header for the model_scenes array change.
;
; STRUCTURE: instances the existing res://assets/terrain/wild_grass/WildGrass.tscn verbatim
; as a child (identity transform), same base-scene-reuse pattern WildGrassCactus.tscn (this
; pass) and WaterLilypad1/2.tscn (Task 8) already use for their own base scenes, plus ONE
; centered desert prop (scale-only transform, no rotation/XZ offset — same convention
; CommonTree1.tscn/Bush.tscn's own "Model" node already uses).
;
; Source: "PalmTree_1.fbx", Ultimate Nature Pack by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — the task
; brief flagged this filename as NOT individually confirmed on disk at plan time (only that
; ASSET_AUDIT.md named "PalmTree" as an available category); on-disk `find` in this task
; confirmed PalmTree_1.fbx exists exactly in the pack the brief guessed (Ultimate Nature
; Pack's FBX/ folder), so no poly.pizza fallback search was needed. (A same-named
; PalmTree_1.fbx ALSO exists in the Nature Crops Pack, part of that pack's separate
; growth-stage series (PalmTree_1..4/_Crop/_Harvested) — the Ultimate Nature Pack's
; standalone tree, not the crop-series one, was used here, matching the "Ultimate Nature
; Pack .../PalmTree_1.fbx" path the brief itself named.) License.txt re-checked at
; `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt` before import, per
; asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate (CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication, same
; boilerplate as every other Quaternius pack in this repo). Recorded in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres (extends that pack's
; existing assets_used list). Flat vertex-color materials ("DarkGreen"/"Green"/"Wood" per
; the source .mtl) — no texture files to carry over, same as Bush.fbx/Rock_Moss_N.fbx
; precedent.
;
; RAW SOURCE LOCATION: copied to res://assets/terrain/wild_grass_palm/PalmTree_1.fbx (a
; single-use prop, not shared across multiple composed scenes, so it lives directly
; alongside this scene rather than in a shared per-model folder — same convention
; CropCactus2.tscn/Cactus_2.fbx already established for single-use crop props).
;
; SCALE: raw PalmTree_1.fbx measured local-space AABB (one-off SceneTree script,
; res://tests/_measure_wild_grass_props.gd, deleted after use, same corner-transform
; procedure Task 8's clearance fix used) = size (2.876911, 4.471397, 2.608991), position
; (-1.267573, -0.02376, -1.074887) — a full-size tree, not a shrub. Scaled to a ~2.2-tile
; target height (scale 0.492013), matching the SAME ~2.2-2.5-tile canopy-height convention
; every Forest tree variant (CommonTree1/2, PineTree, BirchTree) already uses, since this is
; a genuine tree and not a ground-level accent like the Cactus/Coconut siblings in this same
; task. Resulting footprint ~1.416 x 1.284 tile-units — a canopy that overflows the 1x1 tile
; footprint, same as every Forest tree pick already does at this height target (PineTree's
; own header records an analogous ~1.26 x 1.37 footprint at the same height convention; canopy
; overflow onto neighboring tile space is this project's existing accepted convention for
; tree-scale props, not a new decision made here). Y-offset (0.011691 = scale * |raw AABB
; base y|) nudges the model up so its measured base sits exactly on the slab's y=0 top
; surface. FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF:
; whether a full-height palm tree reads correctly standing on a Wild grass tile specifically
; (as opposed to, say, a much shorter "young palm" reading that might fit better against
; wild grass's shorter/scruffier register — WildGrass.tscn's own ~0.065 blade-height
; baseline and its "claim-able but scruffy" framing per Open Question #29), the same open
; question every prior scale/placement judgment call in this pass carries.
;
; NO SLAB WRAPPER NEEDED HERE: same reasoning as WildGrassCactus.tscn's header — the
; instanced WildGrass.tscn already carries its own internal "Slab" wrapper for the
; OcclusionFader exemption mechanism; the palm prop sits as a plain sibling.
